help radix
  {----------- RADIX: Change Input or Display Radix --------}

  {R}ADIX [{B}(bin)/{D}(dec)/{F}(frc or flt)/{H}(hex)/{U}(uns)] [reg[_block]/addr[_block]]...

  {radix}
  Display the default radix currently enabled.

  {radix h}
  Change input radix to hexadecimal.  Hexadecimal constant entries
  no longer require a preceding dollar sign, but any decimal constants will
  require a preceding grave accent.

  {radix f x0  x1}
  Change display radix for registers x0 and x1 to floating point.

  {radix d x:0..10 p:0..10}
  Change display radix for specified memory locations to decimal.

  {radix u x0 x1}
  Change display radix for x0 and x1 to unsigned decimal.
help step
  {----------- STEP: Step Through DSP Program -----------}

  {ST}EP [count] [{CY}(cycles)/{LI}(lines)/{IN}(inst)] [{H}(halt at breakpoints)]

  {step }
  Step one instruction or source line, depending on display mode.
  Display the enabled registers and memory blocks after last instruction.

  {step $50}
  Execute hex 50 instructions or source lines, depending on display mode.
  Ignores breakpoints during execution (use h option to halt at breakpoints).
  Display the enabled registers and memory blocks after the last instruction.

  {step 20 cy}
  Execute 20 clock cycles. Display the enabled registers and memory
  blocks at the end of the 20th clock cycle.

  {step 20 li h}
  Execute instructions corresponding to 20 source lines. Halt at enabled
  breakpoints. Display the enabled registers and memory blocks after the
  last instruction.

  {step 20 in h}
  Execute 20 instructions. Halt at enabled breakpoints. Display the enabled
  registers and memory blocks after the last instruction.

